    pharm: "1. Analgesia: IV Morphine 0.1 mg/kg (5mg) q2-4h PRN (patient-controlled analgesia preferred if available). Oral slow-release Morphine 10-30mg q12h once oral tolerated. Adjunct: Ibuprofen 400mg TID (if no renal impairment). 2. Hydration: IV Normal Saline or Ringer's Lactate at maintenance + 50% (1.5x maintenance). 3. Oxygen: only if SpO2 <95% or respiratory symptoms. 4. Folic Acid 5mg daily. 5. Consider Hydroxyurea (HU) for prevention: start at 500mg daily (if >3 crises/year, after counselling and baseline FBC). 6. If severe or prolonged: consider exchange transfusion (target HbS <30%). 7. Antibiotics: only if fever or infection suspected.",
